    {
      "heading": "Words to equations",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "A plumber charges 60 dollars plus 45 dollars an hour. The bill is 195.",
          "write": "60 + 45h = 195"
        },
        {
          "say": "Let h be the hours. Take 60 from both sides.",
          "write": "45h = 135",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 210,
            "alt": "Bar model with the 60 fee removed",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 40,
                "y": 70,
                "w": 120,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "orange",
                "label": "60",
                "change": "remove"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 160,
                "y": 70,
                "w": 330,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "blue",
                "label": "45h"
              },
              {
                "kind": "line",
                "x": 40,
                "y": 150,
                "x2": 490,
                "y2": 150,
                "color": "black"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 265,
                "y": 185,
                "text": "195 − 60 = 135",
                "size": 24,
                "color": "purple",
                "anchor": "middle",
                "bold": true,
                "change": "add"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Divide both sides by 45. h equals 3 hours.",
          "write": "h = 3"
        },
        {
          "say": "Check in words. 60 plus 3 lots of 45 is 195.",
          "write": "60 + 135 = 195 ✓"
        },
        {
          "say": "Don't just do 195 divided by 45. That forgets the call-out fee.",
          "write": "✗ 195 ÷ 45"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Consecutive even numbers",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Three consecutive even numbers add to 78.",
          "write": "sum = 78"
        },
        {
          "say": "Call the middle one m. The others are m minus 2 and m plus 2.",
          "write": "m − 2,  m,  m + 2",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 230,
            "alt": "Three even numbers around a middle m",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 60,
                "y": 80,
                "w": 140,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "blue",
                "label": "m − 2"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 210,
                "y": 80,
                "w": 140,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "orange",
                "label": "m"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 360,
                "y": 80,
                "w": 140,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "blue",
                "label": "m + 2"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 190,
                "text": "−2 and +2 cancel → 3m",
                "size": 24,
                "color": "purple",
                "anchor": "middle",
                "bold": true,
                "change": "add"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "The minus 2 and plus 2 cancel. 3m equals 78, so m is 26.",
          "write": "3m = 78 → m = 26"
        },
        {
          "say": "So 24, 26 and 28. Not 25, 26, 27, which aren't even.",
          "write": "24, 26, 28"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Work backwards, compare to cancel",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "For a function machine, undo each step in reverse.",
          "write": "last on, first off"
        },
        {
          "say": "Use the opposite operation. Plus undoes minus. Times undoes divide.",
          "write": "+ ↔ −   × ↔ ÷"
        },
        {
          "say": "Two bills with the same number of one item? Subtract them.",
          "write": "compare to cancel"
        },
        {
          "say": "The shared item disappears, and you can find the other.",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 230,
            "alt": "Two bills compared: bananas cancel",
            "items": [
